hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24045","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Zayd, meaning Ibn Aslam, from a man of Banu Sulaym, from his grandfather, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with silver and said: This is from a mine of ours. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be mines attended by the worst of people."
